  "body": "The existing Shx structural-smells-and-boundary-check card calls for two blocking analyzer sections that are absent from the current gate. This planning refinement keeps the complete six acceptance criteria and both original manual hostile checks, with the existing Incoming / P2 / five-point card metadata and original body preserved as an exact byte prefix.\n\nThe proposed design separates portable metric/rule/finding decisions from capture, form-reader, report and exit adapters. It makes Shx-specific thresholds, supported source-completeness evidence, reader semantics, test-layer rules, selector discovery and whole-card sizing explicit review decisions. Existing emitter/CLI/Bash PR 2 and runtime PR 3 stay separately owned; no implementation, narrower substitute, new umbrella card or approval transfer is included.\n\nValidation: the unchanged existing `bin/analyze --strict` completed all seven checks with no blocking findings, including 19 tests / 46 assertions / zero failures. The first own JVM launch refusal and correction are retained. All 111 other inherited identities, both original card/receipt prefixes and all configured engine/event history remain exact. The complete independent store, clean status and full diff hygiene pass. All 49 unique published lossless containers pass size/SHA checks. Actual current Receipt River 154440 source matches all 15 tracked files and validates own declared row 58; 36 inherited refusals remain unchanged. Portable canonical reflection is recognized.\n\nAuthoritative EDN reads under the installed owning artifact remain unavailable; all 66 copied committed fixture inputs remain unchanged. Existing Eta Mu 239 tracks distribution consumption. No deprecated JSON mirror, operational transition or Ready qualification is claimed. Baseline PASS does not qualify either absent checker, future hostile cases, mutations, portability or implementation. Synchronization PR 1, native planning review and lawful readiness remain prerequisites.\n\nOne unpublished private final-proof stream was lost through an own repeated capture label after fetching full history; its prior hash-only history and the limitation are retained. The 49 frozen source containers are unaffected; current complete-history proof is freshly verified. No provider requests, source implementation, shared service, settings or external state changes occurred in this lane.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a design proposal outlining structural reports and namespace-boundary checks, including their expected inputs, findings, and qualification criteria.\n  * Expanded planning notes with scope boundaries, implementation dependencies, and conditions for future readiness.\n\n* **Verification**\n  * Recorded baseline analysis results, evidence limitations, and validation outcomes. No checker, workflow, or runtime behavior changes are included.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
